//? Title: Strand sort: actual greedy extraction and stable merge
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Strand sort repeatedly extracts a nondecreasing subsequence and merges it into
the result. The native trace owns the actual strand, remaining keys and merged
result after each pass.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Start a strand with the first remaining key. Scan later keys, appending a key
when it is not less than the strand tail; retain others for the next pass. Merge
each strand into the accumulated result, preferring the earlier result on equal
keys. Every pass removes at least one key. Sorted data takes one extraction with
n-1 comparisons; reverse data takes n strands and quadratic selected work. The
report counts actual extraction/merge comparisons, not a separate pass-count
simulation.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/strand_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/strand_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::strand_sort_trace(std::vector<int>{3, 1, 4, 2, 5});
    std::print("| actual strand | actual remaining | actual merged result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| `{}` | `{}` | `{}` |\n", s.strand, s.remaining, s.merged);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual input3,1,4,2,5");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} extracted strands", r.strands));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual merged {}", r.values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/strand_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
